  "query_preview": "..\nA low pressure system is on its way into the area, and rain \nshowers with weak thunderstorms have started moving into the west \nand southeast parts of the area. This activity is expected to \nincrease and persist through 16Z, and moderate to heavy rain is \nexpected at times. As the system pivots northeastward, a break in \nthe rain is expected briefly before scattered showers and weak \nstorms move back in after 12 PM. This activity is expected to \nleave the area after 8 PM. Winds will also come up after 8 AM this\nmorning. These west to northwest winds have potential to gust to \naround 45 to 55 mph through about 8 PM before they gradually \ndecrease in the late evening.\n\nThe best chance for rain is through noon today, and the highest\namounts are expected on a line from Malta to Jordan. Up to 9\ntenths of an inch is possible in the northeast, and two tenths to\na half inch in the southeast part of the area. The wind will make\nthe rain do some sideways action, so an extremely sturdy umbrella\nwill be needed. Maybe an umbrella made out of titanium or\nsomething.\n\nThis system will move out late tomorrow evening, but a splitting\nupper trough over the western CONUS will remain. This will\ncontribute to a chance of showers moving into the northwest and \nsoutheast parts of the area. There is indication that any rain\namounts will remain below a wetting rain (one tenth of an inch of\naccumulation).\n\nWeak ridging is expected to move in on Wednesday and last through \nThursday afternoon before the next trough tries to move in from\nthe south on Thursday evening. There is moderate to high uncertainty\non the strength of the trough, so rainfall amounts are not\nreliable enough to talk about in this forecast update.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nThe main deviation was to increase PoPs at various times through\n9 PM this evening.\n\nThere is high confidence in winds across the area, and moderate \nconfidence in rainfall amounts through 9 PM today.\n\nThere is high confidence in timing of the next ridge, and low to\nmoderate confidence on the next trough.",
